                <pb facs="1325" n="1319" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg1319"/>

                <p rendition="#flush">The <hi rendition="#small-caps">President</hi>:</p>
                <p>The Acting Secretary of State has the honor to lay before the President copies of
                    dispatches from our minister at Honolulu, Nos. 57 and 58, dated May 31 and June
                    2, 1894, respectively, in regard to the meeting of the constitutional convention
                    and proposed constitution for the Hawaiian Islands.</p>
                <p>Respectfully submitted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                            State</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-06-23"><hi rendition="#italic">June 23,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
